{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1571","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Sequence of Comparisons"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Once upon a time, Petya had an array of integers $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$. But over time, the array itself was lost, and only $$$n-1$$$ results of comparisons of neighboring array elements remained. In other words, for every $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$n-1$$$, Petya knows exactly one of these three facts:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_i \\lt a_{i+1}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_i = a_{i+1}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_i \\gt a_{i+1}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Petya wonders if it is possible to uniquely determine the result of comparing $$$a_1$$$ and $$$a_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to help Petya determine the result of comparing $$$a_1$$$ and $$$a_n$$$ or report that the result cannot be determined unambiguously."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 500$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of the test case contains the string $$$s$$$ ($$$1 \\le |s| \\le 100$$$), where $$$s_i$$$ is:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"<"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if $$$a_i \\lt a_{i + 1}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if $$$a_i \\gt a_{i + 1}$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"="}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if $$$a_i = a_{i + 1}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single string equal to:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"<"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if $$$a_1 \\lt a_n$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if $$$a_1 \\gt a_n$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"="}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if $$$a_1 = a_n$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if it is impossible to uniquely determine the result of the comparison. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n>>>\n<><=<\n=\n<<==\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n>\n?\n=\n<\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the test cases of the example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" in the first test case, it's easy to see that $$$a_1 \\gt a_4$$$ since $$$a_1 \\gt a_2 \\gt a_3 \\gt a_4$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" in the second test case, both sequences $$$[1, 2, 0, 10, 10, 15]$$$ and $$$[10, 11, 1, 2, 2, 5]$$$ meet the constraints; in the first one, $$$a_1 \\lt a_6$$$, and in the second one, $$$a_1 \\gt a_6$$$, so it's impossible to compare $$$a_1$$$ and $$$a_6$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" in the third test case, we already know that $$$a_1 = a_2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" in the fourth test case, it's easy to see that $$$a_3 = a_4 = a_5$$$, and $$$a_1 \\lt a_2 \\lt a_3$$$, so $$$a_1 \\lt a_5$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1571A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1571/problem/A"}